{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqq2xj787yq","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"code_node layer ships separate map plus direct RAG retrieval validated at k recall ceiling","summary":"Phase 2 code_node layer built and isolated-daemon E2E validated. ARCHITECTURE (as designed in note-mqpzfgjlux8): code_nodes live in their OWN overlay map (lib/overlay.js, keyed code:<file>#<name>), separate from note_nodes and knowledge_nodes, with own event type code_node_upserted, graph-store rehydration, and EMPTY_NODE.code_node — so the dup-judge/note-learner (iterate note_nodes) and delta/dashboard never see them. Unlike knowledge_nodes (structural-expansion-only, score 0.001), code_nodes are DIRECTLY RAG-retrievable: lib/search/memory-search.js scores them by cosine over their pooled vec into the same /search ragResults pool, tagged tier `code`, tunable ORCH_CODE_NODE_WEIGHT; note_nodes scoring is byte-unchanged. Bulk write POST /overlay/code-nodes/bulk mirrors /overlay/notes/bulk exactly (embedBatch in 48-chunks, SKIP dup-guard, ONE epoch bump) into upsertCodeNode. Embed text = `<name> — <signature> in <file>` (lib/node-tags.codeNodeEmbedText, the one shared definition). Ingest helper lib/code-extract/ingest.js: extractRepo().symbols -> payloads -> bulk POST. E2E RESULT (isolated daemon :8799, own ORCH_DATA, models symlinked): extracted 1158 lib/+routes/ symbols (0 parse failures), ingested all 1158, ran the 13-query code-nav corpus -> MEAN SYMBOL RECALL 0.474 @k=10 (in the expected 0.4-0.6 band). KEY FINDING (diagnostic): the k=10 zeros are a RANKING CEILING of single-vec cosine at tight k, NOT a pipeline gap — q07 goes 0.00@k10 -> 1.00@k50 (its symbols rank #12-#39), q09 0.75->1.00, confirming every relevant symbol IS ingested+embedded+retrievable, just crowded below 10. Matches the benchmark note's framing (raw locators lean/lower-recall; full agentic deliver-code search reached 0.583). Tests: test/code-node-bulk.test.js 26/26 (batched, separate map, one-epoch, no dup-guard, i